4. DC-Link and Snubber Capacitance
A. Sizing for Ripple Control
You can estimate DC-link capacitance ( C_{dc} ) as:
[
C_{dc} \ge \frac{I_{pulse} \cdot \Delta t}{\Delta V}
]
Where:
    • ( I_{pulse} ) = worst-case phase current spike (A)
    • ( \Delta t ) = pulse duration (s)
    • ( \Delta V ) = acceptable bus voltage ripple (V)
Typical design targets:
    • ΔV ≤ 5 % of Vbus
    • Pulse durations: 0.5–2 ms for motor phase commutation
    • Add 20–30 % margin for non-ideal ESR/ESL
